From: LM-G820N Developer <dev@lmg820n.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] qcom: fix camera lifecycle and stability issues

Address essential stability and lifecycle defects in the Qcom pipeline
handler and LG AWB algorithms:
1. In lg_awb_colour.h, return neutral ratios { 1.0f, 1.0f } when input.y
   is below 0.001 or green is near zero, avoiding IEEE 754 0/0 NaN
   contamination in dark scenes.
2. In lg_awb_convergence.h, seed history with target gains on initial
   startup when history is empty, preventing NaN division and initial
   gain drops.
3. In qcom.cpp openAncillaryDevices(), downgrade SSC accelerometer
   failure to a non-fatal warning so external sensor daemon timeouts do
   not prevent opening the main rear camera.
4. In qcom.cpp setManualAwb(), explicitly reset awbGainG_ = 1.0 to
   prevent residual green gain from automatic AWB corrupting manual
   colour temperature.
5. In qcom.cpp updateFlashMeasurement(), disengage Torch illumination
   as soon as precapture measurement settles to avoid leaving high-power
   flash LEDs on continuously.
6. In qcom.cpp updateMetadata(), protect ColourGains against green
   division by zero and restrict frameStates_ lookup strictly to cameras
   with autofocus enabled (afEnabled_), ensuring non-AF cameras
   (ultra-wide IMX351 and front IMX520) do not drop all frame metadata.

